  "notes": "FORMAL VOCABULARY:\n{飲酒|いんしゅ} is a formal term often used in legal, medical, and official contexts. In casual conversation, {酒|さけ}を{飲|の}む (to drink alcohol) or お{酒|さけ}を{飲|の}む is more natural.\n\nLEGAL TERMS:\n- {飲酒|いんしゅ}{運転|うんてん} - drunk driving\n- {飲酒|いんしゅ}{検問|けんもん} - sobriety checkpoint\n- {酒気帯|しゅきお}び{運転|うんてん} - driving under the influence\n\nHEALTH-RELATED:\n- {適量|てきりょう}{飲酒|いんしゅ} - moderate drinking\n- {過度|かど}の{飲酒|いんしゅ} - excessive drinking\n- {飲酒|いんしゅ}{習慣|しゅうかん} - drinking habits\n\nJAPANESE LAW:\nThe legal drinking age in Japan is 20 years old ({二十歳|はたち}).",
